Project B (Swig / Python)
=========================

* calculate some observables in Python

-> use swig, Python, numpy, pyevtk, VTK, quadratures

* use swig to generate Python bindings from project A
* calculate basis overlap using non-exact quadratures (check orthonormality) (BONUS: exact)
* calculate observables of the local density state like <A>, <z>, <Q20> in Python (rectangles, quadratures...) (BONUS: exact) (SUPERBONUS: HO)
* estimate the errors associated with the different non-exact techniques
* generate the 3D density in Python from 2D density (C++) (BONUS: no interpolation)
* visualize the 3D density using VTK (Python) or Paraview or POVray
* for the rest of the project, use gitlab PRs only (only one project member with rw) !

Lectures
--------

* project presentation
* python and C++
* swig
* quadratures
* VTK
* paraview ?

Optional lectures
-----------------

* python
* numpy
* venv/pip
* matplotlib
* POVray
